  "collectFramework": {
    "canonicalMoves": [
      {
        "move": "invocation",
        "example": "Omnipotens sempiterne Deus"
      },
      {
        "move": "relative rationale/praise",
        "example": "qui dedisti famulis tuis..."
      },
      {
        "move": "petition marker",
        "example": "quaesumus"
      },
      {
        "move": "desired outcome",
        "example": "ut ... muniamur adversis"
      },
      {
        "move": "conclusion",
        "example": "Per Dominum nostrum ... per omnia saecula saeculorum"
      }
    ],
    "readingRule": "Parse rhetorical moves first, then resolve morphology inside each move, then reread the Collect continuously.",
    "referenceIds": [
      "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1",
      "grammar-nunn-1922",
      "grammar-scanlon-1944",
      "grammar-petitmangin-1930"
    ]
  },
  "learningBlocks": [
    {
      "id": "l30-b1",
      "type": "concept",
      "title": "A Collect has an architecture",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Roman Collects are compact but highly organized. Find the invocation, any relative clause explaining God's attribute/action, the petition, the requested outcome, and the Christological conclusion.",
        "fr": "Les collectes romaines sont brèves mais fortement structurées. Repérez l'invocation, la relative qui expose l'attribut ou l'action divine, la demande, le résultat demandé et la conclusion christologique."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ],
      "localization": {
        "fr": {
          "title": "Une oraison possède une architecture"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l30-b2",
      "type": "collect",
      "title": "Invocation",
      "sourceId": "trinity-collect-l30",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Omnipotens sempiterne Deus gives three coordinated identifying words before the sentence expands. Do not search for a finite verb too early.",
        "fr": "Omnipotens sempiterne Deus donne trois mots d'identification coordonnés avant que la phrase ne s'étende. Ne cherchez pas trop tôt un verbe conjugué."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "trinity-collect-l30",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ],
      "localization": {
        "fr": {
          "title": "Invocation"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l30-b3",
      "type": "collect",
      "title": "Relative rationale",
      "sourceId": "trinity-collect-l30",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "qui dedisti famulis tuis... explains what God has granted. The infinitives agnoscere and adorare depend on dedisti and carry their own complements.",
        "fr": "qui dedisti famulis tuis... explique ce que Dieu a accordé. Les infinitifs agnoscere et adorare dépendent de dedisti et portent leurs propres compléments."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "trinity-collect-l30",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ],
      "localization": {
        "fr": {
          "title": "Motif relatif"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l30-b4",
      "type": "collect",
      "title": "Petition and ut-clause",
      "sourceId": "trinity-collect-l30",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "quaesumus marks the petition; ut ... muniamur gives the requested result. Earlier purpose/result/subjunctive work now becomes part of one real Collect.",
        "fr": "quaesumus marque la demande ; ut ... muniamur donne le résultat demandé. Le travail antérieur sur ut, le résultat et le subjonctif s'intègre maintenant dans une vraie collecte."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "trinity-collect-l30",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ],
      "localization": {
        "fr": {
          "title": "Demande et proposition en ut"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l30-b5",
      "type": "collect",
      "title": "Conclusion",
      "sourceId": "trinity-collect-l30",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "The conclusion identifies Christ and the Trinitarian relation before the final per omnia saecula saeculorum. Treat it as a familiar reusable syntax block.",
        "fr": "La conclusion identifie le Christ et la relation trinitaire avant le per omnia saecula saeculorum final. Lisez-la comme un bloc syntaxique familier et réutilisable."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "trinity-collect-l30",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ],
      "localization": {
        "fr": {
          "title": "Conclusion"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l30-b6",
      "type": "stage-checkpoint",
      "title": "Read the whole Collect without resetting",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "The Stage 6 gate is continuous reading. You may mark clause boundaries, but you must preserve the prayer's rhetorical movement from invocation to conclusion.",
        "fr": "Le contrôle de l'étape 6 exige une lecture continue. Vous pouvez marquer les limites des propositions, mais vous devez conserver le mouvement rhétorique de l'invocation à la conclusion."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ],
      "localization": {
        "fr": {
          "title": "Lire toute l’oraison sans repartir de zéro"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "authenticPassages": [
    {
      "id": "l30-p1",
      "sourceId": "trinity-collect-l30",
      "sourceLatin": "Omnipotens sempiterne Deus, qui dedisti famulis tuis in confessione verae fidei, aeternae Trinitatis gloriam agnoscere, et in potentia maiestatis adorare unitatem: quaesumus; ut, eiusdem fidei firmitate, ab omnibus semper muniamur adversis. Per Dominum nostrum Jesum Christum Filium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitate Spiritus Sancti Deus, per omnia saecula saeculorum. Amen.",
      "instructionalDisplay": "Omnipotens sempiterne Deus, qui dedisti famulis tuis in confessione verae fidei, aeternae Trinitatis gloriam agnoscere, et in potentia maiestatis adorare unitatem: quaesumus; ut, eiusdem fidei firmitate, ab omnibus semper muniamur adversis. Per Dominum nostrum Jesum Christum Filium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitate Spiritus Sancti Deus, per omnia saecula saeculorum. Amen.",
      "translation": {
        "en": "Almighty everlasting God, who hast granted Thy servants, in confessing the true faith, to acknowledge the glory of the eternal Trinity and in the power of Majesty to adore Its Unity: we beseech Thee that, by steadfastness in this faith, we may ever be defended from all adversities. Through our Lord Jesus Christ Thy Son, who with Thee liveth and reigneth in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end. Amen.",
        "fr": "Dieu tout-puissant et éternel, qui avez donné à vos serviteurs, dans la confession de la vraie foi, de reconnaître la gloire de l'éternelle Trinité et d'adorer l'Unité dans la puissance de sa Majesté : nous vous en supplions, faites que, par la fermeté de cette même foi, nous soyons toujours protégés de toute adversité. Par Notre-Seigneur Jésus-Christ, votre Fils, qui vit et règne avec vous dans l'unité du Saint-Esprit, Dieu, pour les siècles des siècles. Amen."
      },
